1
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:10,220
A Pioneer for All People Although he is one of China's most famous

2
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:16,260
scientists, Yuan Longping considers himself a farmer, for he works the land to do his

3
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:17,400
research.

4
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:24,360
Indeed, his sun-burnt face and arms, and his slim, strong body, are just like those of

5
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:29,580
Chinese farmers, for whom he has struggled for the past five decades.

6
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:35,580
Dr Yuan Longping grows what is called super hybrid rice.

7
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:43,040
In 1974, he became the first agricultural pioneer in the world to grow rice

8
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,580
that has a high output.

9
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:51,960
This special strain of rice makes it possible to produce one-third more of the crop in the same fields.

10
00:00:52,680 --> 00:01:00,060
Now more than 60% of the rice produced in China each year is from this hybrid strain.

11
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,180
Born into a poor farmer’s family in 1930,

12
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:10,320
Dr Yuan graduated from Southwest Agricultural College in 1953.

13
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:16,080
Since then, finding ways to grow more rice has been his life goal.

14
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:21,680
As a young man, he saw the great need for increasing the rice output.

15
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:27,740
At that time, hunger was a disturbing problem in many parts of the countryside.

16
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:34,960
Dr Yuan searched for a way to increase rice harvests without expanding the area of the fields.

17
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:57,600
These increased harvests mean that 22% of the world’s people are fed from just 7% of the farmland in China.

18
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:02,440
Dr Yuan is now circulating his knowledge in India,

19
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:07,920
Vietnam and many other less developed countries to increase their rice harvests.

20
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:21,020
Using his hybrid rice, farmers are producing harvests twice as large as before.

21
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:25,620
Dr Yuan is quite satisfied with his life.

22
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:29,060
However, he doesn’t care about being famous.

23
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,620
He feels it gives him less freedom to do his research.

24
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:48,380
Spending money on himself or leading a comfortable life also means very little to him.

25
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:55,840
Indeed, he believes that a person with too much money has more rather than fewer troubles.

26
00:02:56,700 --> 00:03:01,340
He therefore gives millions of yuan to equip others for their research in agriculture.

27
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:04,240
Just dreaming for things, however,

28
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:05,500
costs nothing.

29
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:10,220
Long ago Dr yuan had a dream about rice plants as tall as sorghum.

30
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:17,580
Each ear of rice was as big as an ear of corn and each grain of rice was as huge as a peanut.

31
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:22,720
Dr Yuan awoke from his dream with the hope of producing a kind of rice

32
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:24,320
that could feed more people.

33
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:30,060
Now, many years later, Dr Yuan has another dream:

34
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:34,120
to export his rice so that it can be grown around the globe.

35
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:37,080
One dream is not always enough,

36
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:40,800
especially for a person who loves and cares for his people.
